# shellcheck shell=bash
use flake

# Per-machine answers that are nobody else's: the drive a disk-heavy run should
# absorb, and the lane knobs documented in docs/reference/microvm-verification-harness.md.
# Untracked, and plain `export` lines only — `tests/host/disk-preflight` sources
# this file directly so a lane invoked outside a direnv shell still finds the
# drive, and it has no direnv stdlib to offer.
source_env_if_exists .envrc.local

# Development pins, so a `viv` invoked in this shell evaluates against this tree
# rather than the branch the shipped defaults name. `scripts/baseline-pins` owns
# the reasoning and fails open, and it is evaluated here rather than written into
# `.envrc.local` for two reasons: the store paths move whenever `nix/flake.lock`
# does, so a literal would go stale without saying so, and that file's contract
# is plain `export` lines because `disk-preflight` sources it without direnv.
#
# The devShell's own `viv` pins itself and does not need this. What this covers
# is everything else run from the repository — an installed `viv`, a hand-run
# `nix build`, a lane invoked directly.
eval "$(scripts/baseline-pins)"

# Move the release-kit pin forward, at most once a day per checkout, silently
# when there is nothing to do. A bump leaves a two-file diff in flake.nix and
# flake.lock to review and commit. `RK_DEVSHELL_SYNC=0` in .envrc.local switches
# it off, and a failed bump restores both files rather than leaving them split.
rk devshell sync --apply || true
